# Copy to .env and fill in before `docker compose up --build -d worker`.
# Credentials below are names the Workflow Configuration (`workflow/workflow.yml`)
# refers to: `target.token-env` and `models.<id>.api-key-env`. Values live only
# here, never in the YAML. Upstream reference: coding-agent's compose.yaml and
# docs/ops/workflow-configuration.md at CODING_AGENT_REF.

# Fine-grained PAT with access to {{OWNER}}/{{REPO}} (contents,
# pull-requests, issues: read & write). Named by the Workflow Configuration's
# `target.token-env`.
GITHUB_TOKEN=
# The Target Repository. The Worker reads it from `workflow/workflow.yml`
# (`target.repository`); it is repeated here so the Fleet check and the
# wrong-instance guard (`--expect-repo`) can read it without parsing YAML.
# Never compare or print the tokens of two files: see the create-agent skill.
TARGET_REPO={{OWNER}}/{{REPO}}

# Which commit of https://github.com/lbacik/coding-agent the image builds
# from (branch, tag, or commit SHA; see the `engine` service in
# compose.yaml's build arrangement).
# Default main tracks upstream; pin a tag to freeze the agent's code, then
# `docker compose build` to rebuild against it — no other file needs editing.
# The toolchain (the image's Supported Toolchain Matrix) follows the same
# ref: the `engine` service builds the `deployment` target at this ref, and
# the derived image builds FROM it. Checked by the create-agent skill
# against the target's Project Profile before scaffolding.
CODING_AGENT_REF={{CODING_AGENT_REF}}

# Model credential: set the one the Workflow Configuration names in
# `models.<id>.api-key-env`; leave the others commented out. Which pair the
# ref supports is code-owned (coding-agent
# `src/coding_agent/provider/config.py` for direct pins,
# `docs/ops/workflow-configuration.md`, "Gateway pins", for gateway pins):
# at the documented ref, `anthropic / claude-sonnet-5 / messages` and
# `openai / gpt-5.6-luna / responses` direct, or a `litellm` gateway pin (for
# example `muse-spark-1.3-contributor` at `responses`, reaching the Meta
# route through the gateway).
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# Gateway pin only: the Workflow Configuration's `api-key-env`.
# LITELLM_PROXY_API_KEY=

# Which Workflow of workflow.yml the worker runs (default `implement`).
# Only `implement` is rendered; uncomment only to run another id after adding
# it to the YAML.
# WORKFLOW=implement
# The Workflow Configuration, its prompt files and the reviewed policy are
# baked into the derived image (see the Dockerfile): any edit under
# `workflow/` needs `docker compose build` before the container is recreated.
# There is no config-dir override variable — the package is never mounted.
# Checkout a `validate` run checks against its own Project Profile.
# Uncomment and point at a target checkout when offered that run; there is no
# usable default (see compose.yaml).
# TARGET_PROJECT=
# LiteLLM gateway network (gateway pin only): when the Workflow Configuration
# pins a Model Gateway reachable as a Docker service (for example
# `http://litellm:4000`), the worker joins the gateway's external network
# through compose.coding-agent.litellm.yaml. Uncomment both lines (and set the
# network name) only then; a host-URL gateway needs no overlay, and the
# gateway itself is separate infrastructure this skill never starts.
# COMPOSE_FILE=compose.yaml:compose.coding-agent.litellm.yaml
# GATEWAY_NETWORK=

# Per-Worker resource limits; compose.yaml's x-agent anchor holds the
# defaults below and why. Every service of this Instance gets the same values.
# Uncomment only to change one.
# WORKER_CPUS=1.5
# WORKER_MEM_LIMIT=3g
# WORKER_PIDS_LIMIT=1024
